## Why This Is Asked

Tests fundamental low-level synchronization and memory ordering concepts in a realistic micro-optimization context.

## Key Concepts

- Atomic flags and test_and_set semantics
- memory_order_acquire vs memory_order_release
- Busy-wait with cpu pause for reduced contention
- Backoff strategies to avoid cache-line thrashing

## Code Example

```javascript
#include <stdatomic.h>
#include <immintrin.h>

typedef atomic_flag spinlock_t;
void spinlock_init(spinlock_t* s) { atomic_flag_clear(s); }
void spinlock_lock(spinlock_t* s) { while (atomic_flag_test_and_set_explicit(s, memory_order_acquire)) { _mm_pause(); } }
void spinlock_unlock(spinlock_t* s) { atomic_flag_clear_explicit(s, memory_order_release); }
